'''Krill''' were small [[crustacean]]s that lived in [[water]] in great numbers.<ref name="Chapter 4" /> In the [[ocean]]s of the [[planet]] [[Kamino]], they were a major source of [[Foodstuff|food]] for the semi-aquatic [[aiwha]] [[species]], which had [[baleen]]s in their [[mouth]]s to filter krill out from seawater.<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> On the planet [[Sorgan]], freshwater krill were [[farm]]ed by an isolated [[Unidentified village (Sorgan)|village]], and were used to brew the drink [[spotchka]].<ref name="Chapter 4" />

{{Creature-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Krill were first mentioned in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[2017]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]'', which was written by [[Adam Bray]], [[Tricia Barr]] and [[Cole Horton]].<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> They had previously been mentioned in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in the [[2001]] video game ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Battlegrounds]]''.<ref name="Battlegrounds">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Battlegrounds]]''</ref>

Krill made their first on-screen appearance in canon in "[[Chapter 4: Sanctuary]]," an episode of the [[The Mandalorian Season One|first season]] of the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''.<ref name="Chapter 4" /> The episode aired on [[November 29]], [[2019]].<ref name="Airdate">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|date=2019-09-24|format=[[Wikipedia:PDF|PDF]]|work=[[Wikipedia:Walt Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International|Walt Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]]|pages=[https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf#page=1]|archivedate=20210623202717}}</ref>

